    <main>
        <h1>LeetCode 1401: Circle and Rectangle Overlapping (C++)</h1>
        <div class="problem-description">
            <p><strong>Problem:</strong>
                You are given a circle represented as (radius, xCenter, yCenter) and an axis-aligned
                rectangle represented as (x1, y1, x2, y2), where (x1, y1) is the bottom-left corner and
                (x2, y2) is the top-right corner of the rectangle. Return true if the circle and the
                rectangle are overlapping, otherwise return false. In other words, check if there is any
                point (xi, yi) that belongs to the circle and the rectangle at the same time.
            </p>
            <p><strong>Example:</strong>
                Input: radius = 1, xCenter = 0, yCenter = 0, x1 = 1, y1 = -1, x2 = 3, y2 = 1<br>
                Output: true<br>
                Explanation: The circle centered at the origin with radius 1 touches the rectangle's left
                edge, so they overlap.
            </p>
        </div>
        <div class="code-container">
            <button class="copy-button" onclick="copyCode(this)">Copy Code</button>
            <pre><code class="language-cpp">class Solution {
public:
    static bool checkOverlap(int rad, int xc, int yc, int left, int bottom, int right, int top) {
        left -= xc;
        right -= xc;
        bottom -= yc;
        top -= yc;

        int distSq = 0;

        distSq += (left &gt; 0) ? left * left : 0;
        distSq += (right &lt; 0) ? right * right : 0;
        distSq += (bottom &gt; 0) ? bottom * bottom : 0;
        distSq += (top &lt; 0) ? top * top : 0;

        return rad * rad &gt;= distSq;
    }
};</code></pre>
